     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Maybe you already solved this problem, but everyone currently with the same question, this page will help (it is possible now to use dashboard components in fluidpage) : <a href=\"https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/shinyWidgets/versions/0.4.4/topics/useShinydashboard\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/shinyWidgets/versions/0.4.4/topics/useShinydashboard&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792387614170000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3bKMtRrNTqGLJCJNLlEx5T\">https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/shinyWidgets/versions/0.4.4/topics/useShinydashboard</a> <br><br>Op donderdag 9 maart 2017 15:07:22 UTC schreef msquatrito:</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all,<div>I would like to include some shiny dashboard components, e.g. `box` or `valueBox`, inside a `fluidPage` instead of a `dashboardPage`.</div><div>Unfortunately, they are not displayed properly, e.g. no background for the valueBox, boxes cannot be collapsed, etc.  </div><div>Is there any work around to solve these issues?</div><div>Thanks in advance.</div><div>Massimo</div></div></blockquote></div>"
